{"type":"finding","id":"F-1","ts":"2026-10-21T19:41:30Z","run":"R-20261021-143942-315138","branch":"feat/core-statusline","file":"src/render.rs","line":103,"severity":"nit","category":"logic","title":"truncate sums per-character widths while fit measures whole-string width, so emoji with a variation selector end up wider than max_width","evidence":"render::fit decides a lone segment is too wide with UnicodeWidthStr::width on the whole string (src/render.rs:91), but truncate adds up UnicodeWidthChar::width one character at a time (src/render.rs:111). With unicode-width 0.2.2, U+26A0 U+FE0F is 2 columns as a string but 1 + 0 per character. A model name of four of them with COLUMNS=9 (a budget of 5) renders as four emoji plus an ellipsis, about 9 columns wide.","fix":"Measure the kept prefix with UnicodeWidthStr::width, the same measure fit uses, so a truncated segment never exceeds max_width.","votes":"3/3"}
